{
  "nodes": [
    {"id":"root","type":"text","x":-160,"y":-560,"width":360,"height":140,"color":"5",
     "text":"# app.py\nComposition root.\n`FEATURES = [apps, youtube, opencode, power, ui, graph]`\nEach feature module exposes `routes` + optional `setup(app)`; app.py just wires them into one aiohttp app."},

    {"id":"g-features","type":"text","x":-780,"y":-340,"width":1480,"height":60,"color":"4",
     "text":"**hub/features/** — one module per capability, each its own `web.RouteTableDef()`"},

    {"id":"f-apps","type":"text","x":-780,"y":-260,"width":260,"height":140,
     "text":"### apps.py\nSpawn/stop/proxy the fronted apps (`APPS` registry). Idle reaper. Restart/shutdown endpoints (exit code 42 = relaunch, 0 = stay down)."},
    {"id":"f-youtube","type":"text","x":-500,"y":-260,"width":260,"height":140,
     "text":"### youtube.py\nUpload (`yt_upload.py`, YouTube Data API) + download (`ytdl.py`, yt-dlp+ffmpeg). Download pipeline shares lineage with the standalone **yt-fetch** project (same output dirs)."},
    {"id":"f-opencode","type":"text","x":-220,"y":-260,"width":260,"height":160,
     "text":"### opencode.py\nPer-folder AI coding sessions. `Manager.create()` copies a source into `Agent Code/<name>[-N]`, writes a source marker, launches `opencode serve` on its own port."},
    {"id":"f-graph","type":"text","x":60,"y":-260,"width":260,"height":160,
     "text":"### graph.py\n`/api/graph` — one node per project, auto-discovered (never hand-maintained). Backs the `/graph` D3 UI. Diff/push endpoints for reviewed write-back."},
    {"id":"f-power","type":"text","x":340,"y":-260,"width":220,"height":120,
     "text":"### power.py\nPC power menu (shutdown/restart/sleep/lock), PIN-gated via `HUB_POWER_PIN`."},
    {"id":"f-ui","type":"text","x":580,"y":-260,"width":220,"height":140,
     "text":"### ui.py\nMenu page, offline/dormant page, service worker, favicons. The only thing that renders the shell UI."},

    {"id":"g-support","type":"text","x":-780,"y":-60,"width":1480,"height":60,"color":"3",
     "text":"**hub/** — supporting modules every feature can rely on"},
    {"id":"s-config","type":"text","x":-780,"y":20,"width":230,"height":120,
     "text":"### config.py\nConstants, `APPS` registry, all paths. `hub/local_settings.py` (gitignored) overrides secrets/PIN/machine paths."},
    {"id":"s-platform","type":"text","x":-520,"y":20,"width":230,"height":120,
     "text":"### platform_win.py\nWindows Job Object — every spawned child process dies with the Hub. Single seam, `_assign_to_job`."},
    {"id":"s-proxy","type":"text","x":-260,"y":20,"width":230,"height":120,
     "text":"### proxy.py\nWebSocket-aware streaming reverse proxy. Every fronted app is reached only through this, never directly."},
    {"id":"s-supervisor","type":"text","x":0,"y":20,"width":230,"height":120,
     "text":"### supervisor.py\nStart/stop + idle reaper for proxied apps — spins one up on first request, stops it after inactivity."},
    {"id":"s-lifecycle","type":"text","x":260,"y":20,"width":230,"height":120,
     "text":"### lifecycle.py\nStartup hooks, graceful cleanup, force-exit watchdog (bounded shutdown even if something hangs)."},

    {"id":"g-knowledge","type":"text","x":-780,"y":220,"width":1060,"height":60,"color":"6",
     "text":"**hub/agent_knowledge/** — the knowledge + status layer OpenCode sessions and the graph both read from"},
    {"id":"k-init","type":"text","x":-780,"y":300,"width":250,"height":150,
     "text":"### __init__.py\n`render_agents_md()` — safety rules + wiki-entity summary + skill index, injected into every session's AGENTS.md. Wiki matching: `project_slug` frontmatter first, fuzzy fallback second."},
    {"id":"k-projects","type":"text","x":-500,"y":300,"width":250,"height":150,
     "text":"### projects.py\n`discover_projects()` — auto-scans `git repositories\\` folder layout, never a static list. `discover_orphan_chats()` — Agent Code folders with no resolvable source."},
    {"id":"k-status","type":"text","x":-220,"y":300,"width":250,"height":150,
     "text":"### status.py\n`git diff --no-index` per project vs. its copy (Windows-safe). Reviewed push-back: A/M only, never auto-delete. `compute_project_links()` from real `[[wikilinks]]`."},
    {"id":"k-skills","type":"text","x":60,"y":300,"width":250,"height":150,
     "text":"### skills/\nDomain skill files (frontmatter: name/description/keywords), matched against project name + file extensions. Bodies load on demand, not inlined."},

    {"id":"g-external","type":"text","x":-780,"y":520,"width":1480,"height":60,"color":"1",
     "text":"External — not part of this repo, only ever talked to over 127.0.0.1 (or by path)"},
    {"id":"e-opencode-bin","type":"text","x":-780,"y":600,"width":250,"height":110,
     "text":"**opencode** binary + `Agent Code\\` copies\nLives OUTSIDE `git repositories\\` on purpose — a session's own working copy can never be mistaken for a source."},
    {"id":"e-wiki","type":"text","x":-500,"y":600,"width":250,"height":110,
     "text":"**LLM Wiki** (this vault)\nRead for AGENTS.md summaries + wiki-link edges. The graph's dashed edges show which projects are/aren't documented here."},
    {"id":"e-apps","type":"text","x":-220,"y":600,"width":250,"height":110,
     "text":"**Fronted apps**\nAny app that binds `127.0.0.1` + honours a base-path env var — e.g. Movie Clipper, File Browser."},
    {"id":"e-tailscale","type":"text","x":60,"y":600,"width":250,"height":110,
     "text":"**Tailscale**\nThe only network path in. The Hub is the sole thing meant to face the tailnet; everything else is proxied."}
  ],
  "edges": [
